mplemented orchestrator-directly on the demo (both mechanical applications of the signed-off patterns): (1) shop search field — the query is a local of the session continuation (a \"search\" act), filtering in the pure projection (search commits d2976fb8, merge into master; live-verified: POSTed a search act over HTTP, the subscription re-projects with the query in the field). (2) grid item creation — empty-selection pane is a create form; program emits a :new payload; effects interpreter derives the slug (VM cannot do strings), enforces uniqueness (-N suffix), validates (and now rejects negative prices — a pre-existing parse-price gap the new tests caught), confirms {:saved slug} (commits 8c051dfd4 + fixes 05ac432c3, 1fb5fa23). Live e2e on shiva over real HTTP: create via POST to /grid/k/<token> → \"saved\", the item renders in the grid list, the shop's search finds it, and /data/catalog.edn on the volume contains it (persisted).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13474:Verification: orchestrator-run from worktree root: 39 tests / 550 assertions / 0 failures; kondo clean; live e2e over HTTP on shiva (create → saved → grid list → shop search hit → persisted to volume).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13486:Verification: demo/ clj -M:test 39/550/0; kondo clean on demo/src+demo/test; shiva redeployed from master 9fd907fd: shop 200, grid 200, image 200, datastar.js 200, the persisted \"Dao Star Probe\" creation still in the volume (1 hit).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13497:Done: (1) Oracle pass 5 completed after two operational detours recorded for the pattern library: (a) direct-ssh oracle runs that outlive their ssh session become orphans blocked on dead pipes - oracle passes MUST run in tmux via script files (the third such miss this week is now a rule); (b) the array-comparison nesting fixture HUNG a real PHP docker container for 27 minutes on the first attempt - docker kill freed the pass, and the completed run recorded PHP's actual behavior: :uncaught \"Nesting level too deep - recursive dependency?\" (PHP errors rather than hangs on the compare; the hang was a different fixture shape). Final: 227 targets, 0 failures, 7 RECORD lines - every P3b gate blocker now carries its oracle record, including :closure-call-user-class recording \"8\" from the gate-ordered user-class source (oracle-only until P4). Log attached: collab/oracle-p3b-pass5-php-8.3.35-shiva.log. (2) The fold dispatched to the engineer (resume c61cd179): 7 pins, the compare text matched to the engine's nesting error, :closure-call-user-class flagged oracle-only.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13498:Decisions: hung-container diagnosis belongs in the gate discipline - a stalled docker-php-entrypoint container during an oracle pass means a fixture that hangs real PHP; kill it, record the PHP behavior as the fixture's oracle fact, and note the departure.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13499:Verification: pass-5 counts above from the shiva log; the fold's local gates pending.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13510:Verification: demo/daostar clj -M:test 39/550/0; shiva redeploy from master e39a4494: shop/grid/CJK images 200, no InvalidPathException, persisted probe intact.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13547:Tree: master 13ec8693 (pushed); dao-star-demo = master; worktree detached at master; shiva deploy moved to fresh clone ds3\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13548:Done: Owner asked whether demo/daostar/deps.edn can reference the datomworld GitHub master hash, then requested it. deps.edn now declares datomworld/datomworld as a git dep pinned to bc6a32ea5e1b76dc4ac1f031f1dd71fe3e9878fd (master as of 2026-10-27 noon) with :deps/root \"demo/daostar\" — the manifest inside the checkout whose paths reach the library sources; the trimmed five mvn deps remain; root :paths are the demo's own src/resources only. Self-reference (the pinned manifest IS this file at the pinned sha — the pre-pin version) resolves cleanly. Verified: clj -P resolves from GitHub (public repo, no auth); clj -M:test 39/550/0 from a clean resolution. Consequences: the demo's behavior is frozen to the pinned commit; a library change requires a deliberate sha bump; the main-repo demo/daostar needs the gitignored images copied locally for tests (done; one stray nested dir cleaned). Second owner request: Dockerfile moved to the daostar root (docker build -t dao-star-cart . from demo/daostar), the nested docker/ dir deleted, README keeps the plain-JVM run as the primary path and docker as optional; docker instructions exist in exactly one README. Redeployed on shiva from a fresh clone ds3 at 13ec8693: shop/grid/ASCII image/CJK image all 200, the persisted probe item still on the volume.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13550:Verification: clj -P + clj -M:test 39/550/0 (worktree and main repo after image copy); shiva redeploy verified per curl line above; InvalidPathException count not re-checked this boot (locale fix is in the image).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13577:Tree: master f88fb31a (pushed); dao-star-demo = master; worktree re-anchored; shiva deploy moved to fresh ds3 at f88fb31a\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13578:Done: Owner: pin demo deps.edn to the datomworld GitHub master hash; rename demo/daostar -> demo/daostar-cart; flatten its resources/ (dao_star_cart layer removed: resources/{catalog.edn,public/{images,css,js}}); Dockerfile at the daostar root; docker optional; docker instructions in the one README. The pin works via :deps/root \"src\": a new src/deps.edn at the repo root is the library manifest for git consumers (paths cljc+clj, the five resolvable deps, nothing else), and the demo's deps.edn pins sha fce91d22303f6246c38560ee2f9066f2b2a0fdf9. Verified: clj -P resolves from GitHub with zero errors and no escaping-path deprecations (the old ../ manifest paths are deprecated and were silently dropped by the current tools.deps — the direct cause of the debugging round); clj -M:test 39/550/0; shiva fresh-clone self-contained docker build and redeploy: shop/grid/ASCII/CJK all 200, persisted probe intact.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13591:Verification: 40 tests / 563 assertions / 0 failures; kondo clean; shiva live e2e over real HTTP: posted a tagory act (\"PS4 console\") to a live session — the re-projection shows the chips (all 13 + All), the selected chip highlighted, and exactly 1 item card (the PS4 console item).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13600:Done: The oracle EXECUTED on real Datomic (Local 1.0.301 + client-api 1.0.69, pairing verified from the loaded jars): 110 eligible cases observed identically in the local run and the Docker run on jupiter (108/110 byte-identical observations; rand + row-order differ by nature). Reconciliation committed (docker/oracle/reconciliation.md @e4eed5f5): 28/29 pending cases observed (29th count correction: Phase 3 promoted rules.required-bound-head); 25 conclusive, 3 not comparable (bounds.* DaoSpace-specific limits). Classification: 10 executable cases confirm the contract's stated expectation; 4 agree apart from the documented :db/id pull difference; 3 CONFIRM the Phase 1 conservative find-shape treatment (Datomic's Client refuses scalar/tuple/collection finds); 7 are Datomic accepting what DaoSpace deliberately refuses (all documented rows: :ret ignored, unknown options, :query-stats, negative offset, 5-position patterns, recursive pull, list-form pull); 1 unexpected; 3 not comparable. THE HEADLINE: after the runner's id-mapping fix, ALL 10 re-run executable cases agree — left/right/both/mutual recursion, unbound entry, stratified negation: Datomic's rule semantics EQUAL the Phase 3 tabling semantics on every corpus shape. Recursion through negation is a bare StackOverflowError in Datomic vs DaoSpace's loud pre-evaluation refusal.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13623:Done: Owner: \"the search text is behaving weird. as i type, letters disappear\". Root cause: every keystroke re-projected the whole app div, and the Datastar morph replaced the search input mid-typing — value resets and focus loss. Fix (ab30b6c8): the search input renders ONCE on the begin page (begin-page grew a :pre slot for pre-body markup) as a SIBLING of the patched element; the projection now emits #app-body (header, chips, grid, footer) and can never touch the input; the input debounces at 150ms so fast typing does not storm the boundary. Live-verified on shiva: begin page carries the debounced input and #app-body; the subscription patch targets app-body and contains zero input fields.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13663:Done: Owner: \"the search is non-responsive\" with the browser console TypeError `can't access property \"target\", event is undefined` in datastar.js. Root cause: under data-on:input__debounce, Datastar (RC.7) defers the expression into a setTimeout where the event object is out of scope — every debounced keystroke threw and no request fired. Fix (1592d7acd, message amended 2bb04ee8 after a local-shell $-expansion mangled two words): the input binds the search signal (data-bind:search), the begin page's base signals declare it, and the debounced handler reads $search from the signal store — no event reference. Redeployed on shiva from ds3; live-verified: begin page has data-bind:search and $arg=$search with zero event.target references, and a POSTed search act (\"switch\") filters the live subscription to 1 item card with no input field in the patch.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13674:Done: (1) The P3b re-confirm returned GATE CHANGES narrowed to two docs items + one evidence item, no code, with the review itself constituting the architect sign-off for one docs commit (\"the re-confirm after that commit is a sha check, not another review\"): (a) the engineer's 158-line docs/design/yang.php.md amendment (C24-C29, status note, section 15 narrowing, row 45 rule) was UNCOMMITTED - my \"worktree clean\" claim in the re-confirm brief was wrong, now corrected and the lesson standing; (b) row 43's design text was stale vs the oracle (\"Cannot increment property\" vs \"Cannot increment a reference held by property\"), plus two stale lines in the uncommitted text (pinned count 91 not 83; C29's texts recorded in pass 5, not at the P4 seam); (c) the Dart run had no attached artifact. All three executed: the amendment committed with the corrections applied (b721e1de, pushed), and the Dart log attached as collab/dart3-yang-php-p3b-293b59a0.shiva.log. (2) The sha check dispatched to fable (resume of the gate thread) - its PASSED line triggers the landing.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13689:Next: P4 rounds -> shiva verify -> commit/push -> gates per the plan's checkpoints (oracle recording passes on shiva between rounds). T3 likewise. Both tracks' remaining arcs: P4 S0-S12 with checkpoints A-D; T3 grammar patch -> lowering -> corpus -> gate.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13711:## 2026-10-27 03:1x +0700 — P4 S0-S1 landed on branch (56dfe5a0), shiva-verified; S2 dispatched; T3 round 1 in flight\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13717:Decisions: the shiva p3b clone doubles as the p4 verification clone via a temp branch (p4tmp), then restores to origin/yang-php-p3b detached - avoiding a fourth clone for now; revisit if the two tracks' verifications ever overlap on shiva.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13718:Verification: shiva cljstyle + focused suite at 56dfe5a0.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13720:Next: rounds return -> shiva verify -> commit/push -> next increments (P4: S3 finalization/clone/readonly/shutdown; T3: S0 goldens then class lowering steps).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13722:## 2026-10-27 04:0x +0700 — T3 S0-S1 landed on branch (05b49f4c), shiva-verified green incl. Node lane; S2 + oracle recording dispatched\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13729:Verification: shiva at 05b49f4c (cljstyle rc=0, node-sub pass).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13731:Next: both S2 rounds -> shiva verify -> commit/push -> next increments per the plans' step lists (P4 S3 finalization/clone/readonly/shutdown; T3 S3 class prelude/heritage/brand checks).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13746:Done: (1) P4 S2's shiva verification caught six failures, all