amespace logs /tmp/ds-*.log on shiva; live stale-token curl above; laptop untouched for suites.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13764:## 2026-10-27 06:4x +0700 — concurrency round: P5 plan commissioned (fable), P4-seam compute on shiva, cross-language demo slice dispatched\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13769:Done: three concurrent lanes launched beside the two S3 engineer rounds: (1) the P5 architect commission to fable (session c42e2f91, plan mode) - P5 depends only on P1 per the slice table, so its plan runs during P4 engineering; (2) the P4-seam compute on shiva (tmux p3b-seam): the FULL permutation oracle recording via corpus full + the php-src phpt selection - both were gate-declared P4-seam conditions and are pure shiva compute; (3) the cross-language substrate demonstration (sonnet, session in the xlang prompt; branch yang-cross-lang-demo off master): a TS closure called from PHP-lowered code and the reverse, with the opacity/null non-identity limits pinned as documented expectations - the empirical evidence slice for the section 8.10 story discussed with the owner this session. Operational note recorded: a trailing & inside a backgrounded dispatch DETACHES the child (it survives; the wrapper completes empty) - the failure mode differs from a kill; check process liveness and log growth before re-dispatching, and never re-dispatch under a live session id (the collision error is the tell).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13772:Delegates: claude-fable-5-1 (P5 plan, c42e2f91); claude-sonnet-5-5 (xlang demo; P4 S3 db2452f3; T3 S3 33e13c5d) - all IN FLIGHT; shiva seam compute running.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13773:Next: five lanes settle -> verify each (P5 plan -> review; seam compute -> attach the artifacts; xlang -> shiva verify -> gate-lite since test-only) -> the S3 rounds continue their cycle. OWNER DECISION OPEN: the W0a SQL corpus freeze (dao.wordpress decision 4) remains the biggest available parallel body of work - it needs the owner's go.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:1377