dsg at the tip\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14108:Verification: browser (typing + screenshot above); shiva six namespaces rc=0 earlier this round; app_test on shiva after the count-wait hardening: rc=1 with the shop-nav failure now fixed locally — the final full app_test needs one clean rerun on shiva at the pushed tip (the earlier shiva runs raced overlay debris from my tars; ds3 was force-cleaned).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14110:Next: one clean app_test rerun on shiva at the pushed tip; owner browser pass.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14118:Verification: JVM focused suites after all fixes: yang.clojure-test 27/116, stream-eval 13/309, repl 52/264, encoder 5/16, macro 25/188, latte-oracle 10 assertions — all 0 failures. Full JVM suite (clj -M:test, ~4100 tests) still running in background at log time; NOT yet evidence. Unrun: Node/Dart lanes (no bb/flutter on this seat; per build-n-test.md Gate Ladder, tri-host G1+ and remote execution belong to shiva/jupiter or a delegate), CLJS/CLJD. Commit NOT made: awaits explicit owner authorization (prior \"go\" covered the set-literal unit only).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14122:## 2026-10-28 03:55:00 +0700 — dao.star cart: the grid spreadsheet fully green on shiva (9/317/0); deployed; browser search verified\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14126:Tree: master dd906371 (pushed); deployed on shiva from dsg at dd906371\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14127:Done: The last sequencing defect fixed: the test's next-tok helper read the GRID's stream for the SHOP's nav (and vice versa) — parameterized over the stream. app_test on shiva at the pushed tip: 9 tests / 317 assertions / 0 failures. Redeployed from the same commit. Earlier in the round: the grid spreadsheet (per-cell save on blur; set-semantics tagories/images cells; the mapcat retract fix), responsive mobile/desktop tagories (strip with navigators / drawer), the section title tracking filters, the browser-verified live search, the splash gate with no scrollbars, the TT Game Stock restyle.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14128:Verification: shiva app_test 9/317/0 at dd906371; deployed shop 200.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14138:- **claude session 8f45af4f** (PID 69458, resumed 03:17): the J5 amended acceptance — the engineer was directed at 2026-10-28 03:4x to finish its current gate and move the remaining verification legs to shiva/jupiter per the remote-agent pattern (the owner's laptop-load directive). Its findings file lands when its remote legs complete.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14155:IN FLIGHT — DO NOT TERMINATE (owner instruction): (1) P4 S5 round: sonnet session db2452f3-b62a-4f08-b435-becfd2f1463b RESUMED in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4; typed-property enforcement/declarations/strict_types coded, ~6 uncommitted files; its LOCAL nine-namespace lane still running (build/p4-s5-lane.log). When it reports: shiva verify (the nine namespaces + cljstyle at the new tip), commit FROM GIT STATUS AGAINST THE BRIEF'S FILE LIST (three path-glob misses this tenancy - the standing rule), push, oracle pass for the new :pending fixtures, then next increment per the P4 plan of record checkpoints. (2) T3 S5 round: sonnet session 33e13c5d-025e-4964-8be9-30cb377d8164 RESUMED in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ts-t3; the init-cost probe authored (1 uncommitted file); its JVM lanes running. Same cycle after; the S5 checkpoint's Node/Dart prelude-suite legs are the ORCHESTRATOR's to run on shiva (bb test:sub:cljs/cljd yang.typescript in the ts-t2b or a fresh clone - mind the one-Dart-lane-per-host rule and the npm-ci/gen:antlr fresh-clone prerequisites). (3) shiva tmux lanes: g3m (a full master gate started at e92c206b - NOW STALE, master has moved; treat as point-in-time, re-run if the delta warrants), phpt-select (DONE, artifact committed). The two oracle tmux patterns are in ~/ci/*.sh. (4) The P5 plan v2.1 of record: collab/1793130147000-architect-php-p5-plan-recon.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md - READY; its engineer dispatch waits on P4's SLICE LANDING (the rever