            | gate (f): Dart 4,113 passed, Node on shiva rc=0, 242 namespaces, 0 failures/errors.                 |\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1593:|                                             |                   | macOS arm64 and one Linux host; sanitizer on Linux; long lanes Linux only (shiva, jupiter) under    |\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1648:**`shiva.stigmergy.systems`** (owner: \"leave jupiter out, use shiva\"), run\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1650:`docs/agents/build-n-test.md` (V: `:301-344`); there is no hosted CI. shiva's\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:1792:| Linux host | \"leave jupiter out, use shiva\"        | Linux x86_64 qualification runs on `shiva.stigmergy.systems` through the `~/ci/` scratch-clone setup of          |\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:2052:| W9      | Linux x86_64 machine named as a precondition                                           | §10.2 and §13.1 (shiva via `~/ci/` scratch clones), §8.3 item 5    |\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:2107:| `docs/agents/build-n-test.md:301-344`                | shiva and jupiter; `~/ci/` scratch clones; shiva snapshot lists no Chez or CMake. Confirmed.                    |\ndocs/design/dao.wordpress.md:34:oracle, owner decision B8.1) and MySQL in docker on shiva (the same\ndocs/design/dao.wordpress.md:342:   docker image on shiva).\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '431,480p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; rg -n \\\"constant|unsupported\\\" src/clj/yang/php src/cljc/yang/php | head -100; rg -n \\\"run-php|engine-result\\\" test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj test/yang/php/antlr\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '431,480p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md; rg -n \\\"constant|unsupported\\\" src/clj/yang/php src/cljc/yang/php | head -100; rg -n \\\"run-php|engine-result\\\" test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj test/yang/php/antlr\"","aggregated_output":"## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n\nTwo Linux x86_64 servers run the full suite faster than a laptop. Both are\nreached over SSH as `sto` with key authentication, and both have `mise`, `tmux`\nand `git`.\n\n| Host | Cores / RAM | Toolchain state (server snapshot checked 2026-10-11; repo selection comes from `mise.toml`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n\n**Never test in `~/workspace/datomworld` on either host.** It is a working copy\nthat is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\nowner. Use a scratch clone under `~/ci/` and leave the working copy alone.\n\n### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n\nRsyncing a worktree over the WAN ran at about 150 KB/s (576 MB of tracked files\nwould take about an hour), and an unanchored `--exclude build` also dropped source\ndirectories named `build`, `out` and `target`. Both hosts reach GitHub, so push the\nbranch from the laptop (a feature branch, never master), make one scratch clone on\nthe host from its existing checkout (a local clone takes seconds), and fetch:\n\n```sh\n# once per host: a separate scratch clone, not the working copy\nssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\n  URL=$(git remote get-url origin);\n  git clone -q --no-checkout ~/workspace/datomworld ~/ci/datomworld-<name>;\n  cd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>; git remote set-url origin \"$URL\";\n  git fetch -q origin; git checkout -q --detach origin/<branch>'\n```\n\nTo test another branch later, fetch and check it out in the scratch clone with\n`git fetch origin` then `git checkout --detach origin/<branch>`. A branch that\nwas never pushed cannot be tested remotely.\n\n### Activate the toolchain in the right order\n\nA non-interactive `ssh host cmd` does not load the shell profile, so `mise` and its\ntools are not on PATH. In a script, do this in exactly this order, after the `cd`\ninto the clone:\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\ncd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1                       # trust is per path; a fresh clone is untrusted\nmise install                                    # install versions selected by this checkout's mise.toml\neval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"                       # puts the repo-selected tools on PATH\nmise current flutter                            # verify the selected Flutter version\n```\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2140:                                      {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2761:       (let [e (php/vfind (get c :constants) :name name 0)]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2763:           (php/throw-error \"Error\" (data/str-concat \"Undefined constant \" (get c :name) \"::\" name))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2869:              :consts (php/vfold (fn [acc e] (php/vput acc :name e)) (get st :consts) (get i :constants) 0)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2878:                    (assoc {} :consts (php/or-default (get parent :constants) [])\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2954:                        (php/vfold (fn [a e] (php/vput a :name e)) acc (get t :constants) 0))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3061:              :constants (get st :consts) :props-decl (get st :props)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3584:       (let [e (php/vfind (get c :constants) :name name 0)]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3586:           (php/throw-error \"Error\" (data/str-concat \"Undefined constant \" (get c :name) \"::\" name))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3591:                                               \" constant \" (get c :name) \"::\" name))))))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5047:                                :constants [],\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5061:(defn- constants-form\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5062:  \"The guest map expression seeding `php.rt/constants` from\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5063:   `builtins/constants`, so `defined` and `constant` agree with the\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5081:          (sort-by key builtins/constants)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5127:                 (define 'php.rt/constants (list 'cell/new (constants-form)))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5171:    php.rt/autoloaders php.rt/autoloading php.rt/class-map php.rt/constants\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:215:     ;; the namespace part of a constant name is case-insensitive, the name is not\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:225:     (fn [k] (get (cell/get php.rt/constants) (php/const-key k)))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:233:               (php/throw-error \"Error\" (data/str-concat \"Undefined constant \\\"\" k1 \"\\\"\"))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:240:           (php/throw-error \"E