{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '520,570p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '2088,2120p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '2150,2190p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '390,435p' test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj; git log --oneline -15 -- src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- resolve-global-name\n  \"`{:primary fq :fallback name-or-nil}` for a function (`kind` :function) or\n   constant (:const) name: an import wins, an unqualified name inside a\n   namespace has the global name as its fallback (the two-key lookup of\n   section 7.3), a qualified one resolves as a class name.\"\n  [ctx kind {:keys [segs lead? ns-kw?], :as q}]\n  (if (or lead? ns-kw? (> (count segs) 1))\n    {:primary (resolve-class-name ctx q)}\n    (let [s (first segs)\n          imp (get-in ctx [:uses kind (if (= kind :const) s (str/lower-case s))])]\n      (cond\n        imp {:primary imp}\n        (= \"\" (:ns ctx \"\")) {:primary s}\n        :else {:primary (ns-prefixed ctx s), :fallback s}))))\n\n\n(defn- class-text\n  \"The resolved class name of the type reference `n` (a `typeRef`,\n   `qualifiedStaticTypeRef` or `qualifiedNamespaceName`), `static` and the\n   primitive types as written.\"\n  [ctx n]\n  (if-let [q (find-qname ctx n)]\n    (resolve-class-name ctx (qname-parts ctx q))\n    (leftmost-token-text ctx n)))\n\n\n(defn- constant-node\n  \"The node of a read of constant `q` (parts of its written name). A builtin\n   folds in the global block and at fully qualified reads; an unqualified\n   read inside a namespace is the two-key run-time lookup, builtins\n   included (plan P6 R7).\"\n  [ctx _n q]\n  (let [{:keys [primary fallback]} (resolve-global-name ctx :const q)]\n    (cond\n      fallback (app* 'php/const-get (u/lit primary) (u/lit fallback))\n      (contains? builtins/constants primary) (builtin-constant-node (get builtins/constants primary))\n      :else (app* 'php/const-get-fq (u/lit primary)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Variables\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- simple-var\n  \"The variable name, sigil included, of a `chain` that is exactly one plain\n   variable, else nil.\"\n  [ctx chain]\n  (let [ks (core/kids ctx chain)]\n    (when (= 1 (count ks))\n      (let [o (first (core/kids ctx (first ks)))]\n        (when (p/rule? o \"chainBase\")\n      \"Function__\" (u/lit (or member \"\"))\n      \"Method__\" (u/lit (or fname \"\"))\n      \"Class__\" (if (:cc ctx) (u/v '%cc) (u/lit \"\"))\n      \"Traic__\" (u/lit (if (= :trait (:ckind ctx)) (:cname ctx) \"\"))\n      (unsupported! n :magic-constant))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-constant\n  [ctx n]\n  (let [k (first (core/kids ctx n))]\n    (cond\n      (p/token? k) (u/lit :php/null)\n      (p/rule? k \"literalConstant\")\n      (let [l (first (core/kids ctx k))]\n        (cond\n          (p/token? l)\n          (case (:type l)\n            \"Real\" (float-literal (:text l))\n            \"BooleanConstant\" (u/lit (= \"true\" (str/lower-case (:text l)))))\n          (p/rule? l \"numericConstant\") (numeric-constant ctx l)\n          (p/rule? l \"stringConstant\")\n          (constant-node ctx n {:segs [(:text (first (core/kids ctx l)))]})))\n      (p/rule? k \"qualifiedNamespaceName\") (constant-node ctx n (qname-parts ctx k))\n      (p/rule? k \"magicConstant\") (lower-magic ctx n k)\n      (p/rule? k \"classConstant\") (lower-class-constant ctx n k)\n      :else (core/default-arm diagnostic-ns \"PHP\" unsupported-rules k))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-array\n  \"`[...]` / `array(...)`: items fold over the empty array left to right, key\n   before value, so a duplicate key keeps its first position and the last\n   value. A trailing `[e]` reads the literal.\"\n  [ctx n]\n            (u/v (:gen ctx))\n            (if (= 2 (count es)) (lower ctx (first es)) (u/lit :php/undef))\n            (lower ctx (last es))))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-expression\n  [ctx n]\n  (let [ks (core/kids ctx n)\n        k0 (first ks)\n        cnt (count ks)]\n    (cond\n      (and (= 1 cnt) (p/rule? k0))\n      (case (:rule k0)\n        \"chain\" (lower-chain ctx k0)\n        \"constant\" (lower ctx k0)\n        \"string\" (string-node ctx k0)\n        \"arrayCreation\" (lower-array ctx k0)\n        \"lambdaFunctionExpr\" (lower-lambda ctx k0)\n        \"matchExpr\" (lower-match ctx k0)\n        \"newExpr\" (lower-new ctx k0)\n        \"parentheses\" (lower ctx (first (core/rule-kids ctx k0)))\n        (core/default-arm diagnostic-ns \"PHP\" unsupported-rules k0))\n      (and (= 1 cnt) (p/token? k0)) (constant-node ctx n {:segs [(:text k0)]})\n      (p/token? k0) (lower-prefix ctx n ks)\n      (p/rule? k0 \"assignable\") (lower-assign ctx n ks)\n      (p/rule? k0 \"arrayDestructuring\")\n      (lower-destructure ctx n (pattern-of ctx n k0) (nth ks 2))\n      (p/rule? k0 \"chain\") (lower-incdec ctx n k0 (:type (second ks)) false)\n      (p/rule? k0 \"stringConstant\") (unsupported! n :index)\n      (and (p/rule? k0 \"expression\") (p/token? (second ks) \"?\"))\n      (lower-conditional ctx n ks)\n      (and (p/rule? k0 \"expression\") (= 3 cnt)) (lower-binary ctx n ks)\n      :else (unsupported! n :expression))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Statements\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- echo-nodes\n  [ctx expression-list]\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; S10: permutation corpus and php-src selection\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- read-edn-file\n  [path]\n  (let [f (io/file path)]\n    (when (.exists f) (edn/read-string (slurp f)))))\n\n\n(defn- engine-result\n  \"`{:out :diag :uncaught}` of `source` on the walker, in the oracle's shape, or\n   `{:refused diagnostics}` / `{:threw message}`.\"\n  [source]\n  (try\n    (let [r (h/run-raw source)]\n      (if (:diagnostics r)\n        {:refused (mapv :message (:diagnostics r))}\n        {:out (h/latin1->text (:php/out r)),\n         :diag (mapv (juxt :errno :message) (:php/diag r)),\n         :uncaught (some-> (:php/uncaught r) (select-keys [:class :message]))}))\n    (catch Throwable t {:threw (str t)})))\n\n\n(defn- run-corpus\n  \"Run `programs` against the recorded oracle map: `{:total :compared :mismatches}`\n   where a host throw or a refusal is always a mismatch.\"\n  [programs oracle]\n  (reduce (fn [acc {:keys [id source]}]\n            (let [r (engine-result source)\n                  want (get oracle id)\n                  bad (or (contains? r :threw) (contains? r :refused)\n                          (and want (not= (update want :diag vec) (update r :diag vec))))]\n              (cond-> (update acc :total inc)\n                want (update :compared inc)\n                bad (update :mismatches conj [id r]))))\n          {:total 0, :compared 0, :mismatches []}\n          programs))\n\n\n(deftest permutation-corpus-quick-test\n  (let [oracle (read-edn-file \"test/yang/php/antlr/permutation_oracle_quick.edn\")\n        {:keys [total compared mismatches]} (run-corpus (perms/quick) oracle)]\n    (is (= (* 2 (count perms/quick-ids)) total))\n    (is (empty? mismatches) (pr-str (take 3 mismatches)))\nedc50134 fix(yang.php): admit foreign yang.call cells\n3321ecee fix(yang.php): preserve by-ref foreach cursor on unshift\nc7c90249 fix(yang.php): repair typed byref and closure scope handling\n0591a64a feat(yang.php): P4 S8 — the generator runtime (partial, kimi session hit its 5-hour limit)\n39fe7ad5 feat(yang.php): P4 S7 — the typed-reference enforcement gap fix, the row-47 property-reference lowering, the S7 generator fixture drafting\n6e49eb06 feat(yang.php): P6 S4-S5 — the loader arms, the namespace resolution, the R7 constants amendment implementation\nca8bbc07 feat(yang.php): P6 S3 — the autoload class map, the computed-path diagnostic, the constants two-key path\ne728f6fe feat(yang.php): P6 S0-S2 — the include/require lowering arms, the constants two-key path, the fixture authoring\n0455d5b1 test(yang.php): the checkpoint-B fixture package — the audit's gaps authored\n5a3783be feat(yang.php): P4 S6 — declarations, strict_types, exception conversion, closure scope\nc52131cc feat(yang.php): P4 S5 review rounds — typed-reference membership, by-ref ownership, defaults, awaiting-oracle gate, oracle uncaught parsing\n3499e218 feat(yang.php): P4 S5 — typed-property enforcement, declarations, strict_types\nb28c3a7d feat(yang.php): P4 checkpoint-A reconciliation — the review's four items + the pass-6 fold\n2f7f4078 feat(yang.php): P4 S4 — exceptions as throwables, throw, try/catch/finally, match on objects\n690b4cd3 feat(yang.php): P4 S3 — finalization, clone, readonly, shutdown; S2 property-write shadowing fix\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
