{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '155,190p' test/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc; sed -n '1500,1535p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '165,195p' test/yang/php/antlr/include_test.clj;\"","aggregated_output":"  (testing \"an undeclared static property refuses\"\n    (is (= \"Access to undeclared static property A::$q\"\n           (uncaught-message (seq-forms (declare-form {:name \"A\"})\n                                        '(php/class-static-cell (php/class-lookup \"A\") \"q\")))))))\n\n\n(deftest constants-test\n  (testing \"a constant thunk runs once; interface and inherited constants are visible\"\n    (is (= \"ev,3,3,k\"\n           (run (seq-forms\n                  (declare-form {:name \"I\", :kind :interface, :consts [{:name \"K\", :value \"k\"}]})\n                  (declare-form {:name \"A\", :interfaces [\"I\"],\n                                 :consts [{:name \"X\", :thunk '(fn [] (do (php/echo \"ev,\") 3))}]})\n                  (declare-form {:name \"B\", :parent \"A\"})\n                  (str-of '(php/to-string (php/class-const (php/class-lookup \"A\") \"X\"))\n                          '(php/to-string (php/class-const (php/class-lookup \"B\") \"X\"))\n                          '(php/to-string (php/class-const (php/class-lookup \"B\") \"K\"))))))))\n  (testing \"an undefined constant refuses\"\n    (is (= \"Undefined constant A::Z\"\n           (uncaught-message (seq-forms (declare-form {:name \"A\"})\n                                        '(php/class-const (php/class-lookup \"A\") \"Z\")))))))\n\n\n(deftest methods-and-abstracts-test\n  (testing \"own methods override inherited ones and keep their declaring class\"\n    (is (= \"B,A,2\"\n           (run (seq-forms\n                  (declare-form {:name \"A\", :methods [{:name \"f\", :code \"a\"} {:name \"g\", :code \"ag\"}]})\n                  (declare-form {:name \"B\", :parent \"A\", :methods [{:name \"F\", :code \"b\"}]})\n                  (str-of (method-field \"B\" \"f\" :declaring)\n                          (method-field \"B\" \"g\" :declaring)\n                          '(php/to-string (data/count (get (php/class-lookup \"B\") :methods)))))))))\n  (testing \"an unimplemented abstract (or interface) method refuses the concrete class\"\n    (is (= (str \"Class B contains 1 abstract method and must therefore be declared \"\n                \"abstract or implement the remaining methods (A::f)\")\n           (uncaught-message (seq-forms (declare-form {:name \"A\", :abstract? true,\nunder a ticks profile only (P7-b).\n\n### 7.3 Scope analysis\n\n`yang.php.antlr.scope`. Scopes are the unit (global) and each function,\nmethod, closure and arrow function. Each records `{:kind :params :assigned\n:statics :globals :uses :arrow-captures :dynamic? :this?}`, with by-reference\nand variadic flags on parameters and `{:name :ref?}` per `use`. `$this` is a\nparameter of methods. Arrow functions compute `:arrow-captures` as the free\nvariables of their body that the enclosing scope binds. `:dynamic?` follows\nsection 3.3. Superglobals resolve to `$GLOBALS` entries everywhere.\n\nName resolution for functions, classes and constants is compile-time:\n`namespace` and `use` statements resolve every unqualified name to a fully\nqualified name by PHP's rules. Functions and constants fall back to the global\nnamespace at run time, which the lowering encodes as a two-key lookup,\n`php/fn-lookup \"ns\\\\f\" \"f\"` and `php/const-get \"ns\\\\C\" \"C\"`. Builtin\nconstants fold in the global block and at fully qualified reads. An\nunqualified constant read inside a namespace uses the two-key lookup,\nincluding builtin names, so a namespace-local declaration can shadow a\nbuiltin. `use const` resolves the read to its imported fully qualified name.\n\n## 8. The lowering-arms inventory\n\n+------------+--------------------------------+--------------------------------+\n| Group      | Arms                           | Lowering                       |\n+============+================================+================================+\n| Output     | `echo`, `print`, `inlineHtml`; | `php/echo` appends to the      |\n|            | `printf`, `sprintf`,           | output-buffer stack            |\n|            | `number_format` (prelude)      |                                |\n+------------+--------------------------------+--------------------------------+\n| Variables  | `$x`, `$this`,                 | `php/local-get` or `cell/get`  |\n|            | `$GLOBALS[...]`, superglobals, | through the marker deref;      |\n|            | `$$x` (dynamic profile, P9),   | writes through `php/assign`    |\n|            | `list()`/`[]` destructuring    | (section 4)                    |\n|            | with keys and references       |                                |\n\n\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; P6 S3-S5: namespaces, constants, the autoload class map\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- lowered-text\n  \"The lowered tree of `src` as a string, to assert what it contains.\"\n  [src opts]\n  (pr-str (:ast (lower/lower-program (cst/parse-source src) (assoc opts :prelude :linked)))))\n\n\n(deftest builtin-constants-fold-only-where-php-folds-test\n  (testing \"the global block and fully qualified reads fold to the literal\"\n    (doseq [src [\"<?php echo PHP_EOL;\" \"<?php namespace A; echo \\\\PHP_EOL;\"]]\n      (is (not (re-find #\"const-get\" (lowered-text src {}))) src)))\n  (testing \"an unqualified read inside a namespace is the two-key lookup, no literal folded\"\n    (let [t (lowered-text \"<?php namespace A; echo PHP_EOL;\" {})]\n      (is (re-find #\"php/const-get\" t))\n      (is (re-find #\"A\\W+PHP_EOL\" t))))\n  (testing \"a name in the const import table is a fully qualified read\"\n    (let [t (lowered-text \"<?php namespace A; use const B\\\\X; echo X;\" {})]\n      (is (re-find #\"php/const-get-fq\" t))\n      (is (re-find #\"B\\W+X\" t)))))\n\n\n(deftest namespace-block-rules-test\n  (doseq [[src msg]\n          [[\"<?php namespace A; namespace B { }\" #\"Cannot mix bracketed\"]\n           [\"<?php echo 1; namespace A;\" #\"very first statement\"]\n           [\"<?php namespace A { } echo 1;\" #\"No code may exist outside\"]]]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
