4/F5/F6/F9/F10, error taxonomy with cognitect anomaly categories, sizing guidance, conformance corpus spec, re-ranked phases 0→1→4→2→3→5 — bounded execution pulled ahead of rules for the web-app consumer, ETA unchanged 44-76 agent-hours). Unit 2: dispatched Phase 0 engineer leg per the doc's amended deliverable table (frozen datomic-q-v1 corpus + loader + conformance harness + JVM oracle runner + deps.edn dev alias) to claude-opus-5-5, fresh session, acceptEdits, bounded to 8 artifact paths.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:12652:Done: Phase 0 engineer leg delivered (opus-5.5, session 6e84b906): frozen datomic-q-v1 corpus (80 cases / 28 contract points / 9 fixtures; 31 executable, 9 difference, 6 refusal, 34 pending), portable fixture loader, conformance harness with digest pinning, JVM oracle runner (safe-output! guard, --backend unselected smoke = 77 pending / 3 not-eligible), deps.edn :oracle dev alias. Orchestrator verification: G0 16 tests / 39 assertions / 0 fail reproduced; scope = exactly 8 artifacts; errata E2 (string query -> #{[]}) and E5 ((min 2 ?a) -> #{[nil]}) reproduced live. Independent review routed to glm-5.3 (family-independent vs opus; argon status unverified post-reset). Reviewer's plan-mode pause resumed with approval (acceptEdits + explicit no-repo-edit constraint); tree audit confirmed zero reviewer edits. Verdict: ENDORSE WITH CHANGES — all five acceptance criteria met, every implementer claim reproduced, five P3 findings (slice-size comparator latent gap; pull-option cases pin list-shape refusal while the nested-vector form IS honored — orchestrator confirmed the code branch parse-attr-options query.cljc:610/:637; pull.reverse-attribute unjustified clj-only; README oracle line -M:test:oracle hijacked by test main-opts; missing use-fixtures :once digest re-assert). All five accepted; fix round dispatched on the RESUMED opus session (context continuity) with same file authority.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13417:Next: PHASE 5 dispatch — Docker oracle environment on jupiter (docker/oracle/Dockerfile + runner --backend :datomic-local with com.datomic/local 1.0.301; :storage-dir :mem), oracle execution of the 29+ pending cases, observations to the separate output file, promotion as a reviewed human step, final compatibility matrix + doc status flips. This is the final phase; after it, the track reports qualified-except-any-residual and the owner decides on pushing.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13600:Done: The oracle EXECUTED on real Datomic (Local 1.0.301 + client-api 1.0.69, pairing verified from the loaded jars): 110 eligible cases observed identically in the local run and the Docker run on jupiter (108/110 byte-identical observations; rand + row-order differ by nature). Reconciliation committed (docker/oracle/reconciliation.md @e4eed5f5): 28/29 pending cases observed (29th count correction: Phase 3 promoted rules.required-bound-head); 25 conclusive, 3 not comparable (bounds.* DaoSpace-specific limits). Classification: 10 executable cases confirm the contract's stated expectation; 4 agree apart from the documented :db/id pull difference; 3 CONFIRM the Phase 1 conservative find-shape treatment (Datomic's Client refuses scalar/tuple/collection finds); 7 are Datomic accepting what DaoSpace deliberately refuses (all documented rows: :ret ignored, unknown options, :query-stats, negative offset, 5-position patterns, recursive pull, list-form pull); 1 unexpected; 3 not comparable. THE HEADLINE: after the runner's id-mapping fix, ALL 10 re-run executable cases agree — left/right/both/mutual recursion, unbound entry, stratified negation: Datomic's rule semantics EQUAL the Phase 3 tabling semantics on every corpus shape. Recursion through negation is a bare StackOverflowError in Datomic vs DaoSpace's loud pre-evaluation refusal.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:14156:QUEUED WORK (the successor's board, in order): (1) process the two S5 rounds per the cycles above; (2) P4 continues S6+ per the plan's checkpoints (B at the S6 boundary