{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_131","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short && git log -2 --oneline && git diff --check HEAD && sed -n '1,180p' collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"?? collab/1793496000000-engineer-p4-checkpointB-fold.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n?? collab/1793500000000-engineer-p4-objects-defects.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n?? collab/1793506000000-engineer-p4-heap-fixture.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n?? collab/1793515000000-engineer-p4-leak-fix.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\n?? collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n?? collab/1793550000000-engineer-p4-retier.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n?? collab/1793560000000-engineer-p4-foreach016.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n?? collab/1793660000000-engineer-p4-yangcall-conformance.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n?? collab/1793700000000-engineer-p4-foreign-admission.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\n?? collab/1793740000000-engineer-p4-e2e-triage.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\nbf8c9c20 fix(yang.php): refuse unresolved global constants\n6dee9f26 test(yang.php): record PHPT quick mismatch manifest\n# P4 e2e red triage\n\n## Bare constant refusal\n\n`constant-node` lowered unresolved unqualified constants in the global\nnamespace to `php/const-get-fq`. That moved `<?php echo FOO;` from the required\nlowering refusal into runtime undefined-constant handling, so\n`refusals-are-named-test` saw no `:yang.php/unsupported` diagnostic. The\nlowerer now refuses that global bare-name case with `:construct :constant`;\nnamespace fallback and qualified runtime lookups remain intact.\n\nFocused verification: `refusals-are-named-test`, 1 test / 22 assertions / 0\nfailures / 0 errors.\n\n## PHPT quick mismatch disposition\n\nAdded `test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn`. The quick\nselection test compares the exact observed failing entry IDs against the\nmanifest, checks every recorded PHPT description, validates the per-feature\ncounts, and asserts the unsupported count. GC and foreach rows name their\nengine work items. This keeps a change from silently removing or adding a\nmismatch while allowing the selection to report its known gaps honestly.\n\nAt this tree, the selected 271 entries report 108 pass, 58 unsupported, and\n105 manifested failures. The previous 115-failure / 48-unsupported report\npredates the bare-constant diagnostic fix; ten constant cases now refuse\nduring lowering. The 105 failure IDs are distributed as follows:\n\n| Feature | Count |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Zend regression cases | 70 |\n| GC cycle collection | 10 |\n| Foreach mutation/reference semantics | 11 |\n| Named parameter binding | 3 |\n| Unset CV behavior | 4 |\n| Array references | 1 |\n| Pass by reference | 5 |\n| Array internal pointer | 1 |\n\n## Thrown error\n\nThe requested quick namespace rerun completed without a thrown test error:\n20 tests / 1,116 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors. The earlier single error\nwas not reproduced at this tip; this clean run does not identify its original\nstack. The PHPT worker catches engine throws and classifies them as entry\nfailures, so the prior error was outside that per-entry catch.\n\n## `gc_013` oracle cross-check\n\nThe pinned row is `Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt`; source builds 10,001 self-reference\ncycles, then prints the result of `gc_collect_cycles() > 0` followed by `ok`.\nThe pinned expectation is `bool(true)\\nok`. `phpt/matches-expect?` trims\ntrailing whitespace and compares the actual body, so the recorded source and\ncomparison shape are consistent on inspection.\n\nOn shiva, ran the exact pinned source through `docker run --rm -i\nphp:8.3.35-cli` under `timeout 300`. The real oracle printed:\n\n```text\nbool(true)\nok\n```\n\nThis matches the recorded pin exactly. The local engine stress test is running\nseparately. It completed in about six minutes with\n`{:out \"\", :diag [], :uncaught {:class \"Error\", :message \"Call to undefined function gc_collect_cycles()\"}}`.\nThe three-way result is therefore:\n\n| Source | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Pinned `phpt_selection.edn` | `bool(true)\\nok` |\n| Docker PHP 8.3.35 on shiva | `bool(true)` then `ok`; matches pin |\n| Engine | Empty output, then uncaught `Error: Call to undefined function gc_collect_cycles()` |\n\nAdded this as `:slow-known-gaps` in the mismatch manifest, with the oracle pin,\nengine result, and named GC work item. The slow PHPT stress test checks this\nrecorded result explicitly. Proposed gap wording: **“PHP cyclic garbage\ncollection is not implemented; `gc_013` self-referential cycles are not\ncollected, so `gc_collect_cycles()` does not return a positive cycle count.”**\n\n## Verification\n\n- PHP e2e quick namespace: 20 tests / 1,116 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors.\n- PHPT quick manifest test after adding the slow `gc_013` known-gap row: 1\n  test / 5 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors (271 entries: 108 pass, 58\n  unsupported, 105 manifested failures).\n- `gc_013` engine stress test: one expected known-gap mismatch with the exact\n  recorded engine result above; its slow test now asserts that result and the\n  pinned oracle text.\n- `cljstyle check` on the changed Clojure files: clean.\n- clj-kondo on the changed Clojure files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n- PHP literal/runtime, class model, include, lower-portable, and scope consumers:\n  46 tests / 1,975 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors.\n- The full `bb test:sub:clj yang.php` attempt was stopped after 13 minutes\n  without a summary in e2e; the standalone e2e gate and focused consumers above\n  completed successfully.\n\n## Commits\n\n- `6dee9f26 test(yang.php): record PHPT quick mismatch manifest`\n- `bf8c9c20 fix(yang.php): refuse unresolved global constants`\n\nBoth commits are on `yang-php-p4`; neither was pushed. This findings file is\nuncommitted as requested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
